# Use shadcn/ui Components

When building UI, always prefer shadcn/ui primitives from `@repo/ui` over custom implementations.

## Importing

```tsx
// Good - use shared shadcn component
import { Button } from "@repo/ui/button";

// Bad - hand-roll a button in the app
const Button = ({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) => (
  <button className="...">{children}</button>
);
```

## Adding a new shadcn component

1. Run from `packages/ui/`:

```sh
 npx shadcn@latest add <component>
```

Re-export from `packages/ui/src/<component>.tsx`.

1. Add `"use client"` if it uses client-side hooks.
2. Import in apps as `@repo/ui/<component>`.

## Key points

- Check `packages/ui/src/` for existing components before creating new ones.
- Do not duplicate shadcn primitives in app-level code.
- Customize shadcn components by editing the source in `packages/ui/src/`, not by wrapping them.
